    "body": "## Summary\n\n**ADR-042 — `position: relative` + `position: absolute`.** Three commits on one branch, merged only after Commit 2's PNG verification.\n\n**Closes three ADRs' open items at once:**\n- ADR-033: `relative` and `absolute` were stored but treated as static; now implemented\n- ADR-041: pseudo synthesis deferred (needs absolute positioning); Commit 2 delivers it\n- ADR-040: h1 underline prediction (mechanism corrected in ADR-041, visually achieved here)\n\n## Commits\n\n| # | Scope | Status |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | **Relative + absolute layout** (behavior change, no first-viewport delta) | ✅ Green — 531 / 2035 tests pass, +13 new |\n| 2 | **Pseudo synthesis** (visible: title underline appears) | ⏳ Pending — PNG verification before merge |\n| 3 | **Docs** (ADR-042 → Implemented, ADR-033/041 post-notes) | ⏳ Pending |\n\n## Measurement (Wikipedia CSS, 2026-10-28)\n\n| Position | Wikipedia uses | Status |\n|---|---|---|\n| `absolute` | 19 | ✅ Commit 1 |\n| `relative` | 22 | ✅ Commit 1 (containing block marker) |\n| `fixed` | 3 | Untouched (ADR-033) |\n| `sticky` | 2 | ⏳ Deferred |\n\n**First-viewport absolutes: 2** — `.vector-page-titlebar::after` (target), `.vector-toc-toggle` (`display: none`).\n\n## Commit 1 details\n\n- `LayoutBox::is_containing_block` (set when `position != static`)\n- Block dispatch collects absolute children, positions after normal children finish\n- All four offsets (`top`/`bottom`/`left`/`right`) with proper auto/over-constrained rules\n- Width/height stretch when left+right or top+bottom both set\n- Explicit width/height preserved when only one axis is set\n\n**Fallback**: parent not positioned → absolute child treated as static (ADR-033 behavior preserved). ADR-033's `test_layout.cpp:1721` (parent = body, not positioned) still passes.\n\n## Commit 2 scope (visible delta)\n\n- Pseudo synthesis after normal children complete\n- `content: ''` → zero-width box, positions per absolute rules\n- `content: 'literal'` deferred (inline path — different code path)\n- Title \"HTML\" underline appears (1px bar at titlebar bottom)\n- **Render-and-inspect PNG required before merge** (ADR-039 lesson codified)\n\n## Deferred (enumerated in ADR-042)\n\n- Flex/grid parent absolutes (v1 handles block parents only)\n- Multi-level containing block walk-up\n- `top`/`left` visual offsets on `position: relative`\n- Percentages in offsets (needs `parent_content_height`)\n- `position: sticky` (needs scroll state)\n- `content: 'literal text'` pseudo synthesis\n- `content: attr() / counter() / url()` (ADR-041 deferred)\n\n## Test count\n\n- Before: 518 cases / 1980 assertions\n- After Commit 1: **531 cases / 2035 assertions** (+13 / +55)\n\n## Reviewer checklist\n\n- [ ] **Narrowed scope is honest** — block-parent absolutes only in Commit 1. Flex/grid parent absolutes deferred (would need 15+ anchor changes across dispatch paths). Comfortable?\n- [ ] **Explicit width/height parse fallback** — box.width/height not finalized at abs-positioning time, so we parse from style directly. Works for all test cases. Acceptable?\n- [ ] **ADR-033's stale test preserved** — test named \"v1\" still passes because its parent isn't positioned. Not updated — still correct for its specific case. Agree?\n- [ ] **Pseudo synthesis deferred to Commit 2** — keeps behavior-only and visible-delta separate. Agree?\n- [ ] **PNG verification gates merge** — Commit 2 must show title underline before PR merges.\n\n## DO NOT MERGE until Commit 2's PNG verification passes.\n\nRefs #209",
